    "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nThis PR refines the ACE specification text around `*crdirty` semantics, aiming to avoid redundant access-trap statements, broaden `scrdirty` availability, reserve unused bits on RV64, and clarify that Dirty tracking may be imprecise (only instructions that *do* change state must set Dirty).\n\n**Changes:**\n- Reword `scrdirty`/`vscrdirty` definitions (including WPRI upper bits on RV64 and updated “Clean→Dirty” conditions).\n- Remove the `ace.clear` rule text about setting `*crdirty` Dirty.\n- Add additional commentary in the lazy-loading section about imprecise dirty tracking and possible lazy-store optimizations.\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/riscv/riscv-high-assurance-cryptography/new/main/.github/instructions?filename=*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
